    "narrative": "LawDog enters the August 2nd slate with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (80.87) and **Bryce Harper** (78.75) anchoring the offense as our clear-cut elite starts. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is in an ideal spot against Me Kelly, who carries a shaky 5.13 xERA; the combination of a favorable matchup and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** batting second in the order provides him the highest upside for RBI and runs today. Similarly, **Bryce Harper** benefits from an elite park factor (+16%) and a favorable matchup against Bradish. We are also leaning heavily into the speed-to-base potential of **Masyn Winn** (64.31). Though facing a veteran like Scherzer, **Masyn Winn** receives a significant boost from the pitcher's slow delivery, which maximizes his stolen base potential\u2014a crucial metric for us given the scarcity of the category in our 5x5 format.\n\nWe are navigating several complex platoon dynamics, most notably with **Gleyber Torres** (67.01) and **Lawrence Butler** (73.47). **Gleyber Torres** enjoys a massive 13% boost from his favorable L/R platoon matchup and leadoff placement, while **Lawrence Butler** utilizes a similar platoon advantage to maintain his strong efficiency score. Conversely, we\u2019ve exercised caution with **Dylan Beavers** (52.50). While the park factor is enticing, he faces a daunting matchup against Wheeler, whose elite pitch mix and hold-rate suppress **Dylan Beavers**\u2019 stealing opportunities, keeping him strictly in the marginal-to-strong category. \n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Geraldo Perdomo** (44.54). He remained in consideration until the final pass, but ultimately lost out to the superior power-hitting matchups of our utility slots. His low score was driven primarily by a tough outing against a high-skill arm in Williams and a lack of the high-ceiling platoon advantages enjoyed by the rest of the lineup. As a reminder, **Yainer Diaz** is currently listed as a scratch from the lineup; we have moved him to the bench to preserve our game caps while we monitor his status for a potential pinch-hit appearance. Ensure your rosters are locked by first pitch.",
